{"id":"20260830T072904.919326656Z-f2e44c6a","time":"2026-08-30T07:29:04.919326656Z","session_id":"session-20260830T072521.605271812Z","task_id":"task-1788074721605515483","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  Fix the candidate-identity behaviour when validation mutates candidate bytes, such as when a configured formatter changes a file. The exact candidate tree bound to review must represent the post-validation content the reviewer actually receives. If that exact reviewed state is accepted and does not subsequently move, canonical candidate minting must succeed for that state. A candidate that changes after the state bound to the verdict must still be refused rather than silently rebound. Add a regression test using a validation formatter that actually mutates candidate content and proves the end-to-end identity behaviour. Preserve the existing fail-closed behaviour for candidate movement and do not weaken review-to-tree or base-to-candidate identity checks. Choose the implementation that best preserves the existing authority and identity model; the task does not prescribe where candidate state should be re-measured.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] The workflow currently captures the candidate before validation, validation may replace the diff after a formatter mutation, and the later review binding still uses the earlier capture tree. (internal/workflow/engine.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] CandidateCapture derives the review diff from its frozen tree and carries the corresponding changed-path set, allowing one measurement to supply all three downstream identity fields. (internal/gitx/capture.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Canonical minting already re-measures the worktree, requires equality with the verdict-bound tree, parents the commit on the recorded base, and verifies both relationships. (internal/workflow/mint.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Existing mint tests separately prove successful exact identity creation and refusal when the candidate moves after review. (internal/workflow/mint_test.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei requires reviewers to judge the whole candidate and requires adversarial verdicts to bind to the revision actually read. (candidate review identity) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Scoped preflight classifies this two-file change as architecture-sensitive with high confidence and local blast radius. (internal/workflow/engine.go and internal/workflow/mint_test.go) — source: graph\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: bounded-knowledge-gap\n"}
