{"id":"20260830T073746.482190739Z-a5333447","time":"2026-08-30T07:37:46.482190739Z","session_id":"session-20260830T072521.605271812Z","task_id":"task-1788074721605515483","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  Fix the candidate-identity behaviour when validation mutates candidate bytes, such as when a configured formatter changes a file. The exact candidate tree bound to review must represent the post-validation content the reviewer actually receives. If that exact reviewed state is accepted and does not subsequently move, canonical candidate minting must succeed for that state. A candidate that changes after the state bound to the verdict must still be refused rather than silently rebound. Add a regression test using a validation formatter that actually mutates candidate content and proves the end-to-end identity behaviour. Preserve the existing fail-closed behaviour for candidate movement and do not weaken review-to-tree or base-to-candidate identity checks. Choose the implementation that best preserves the existing authority and identity model; the task does not prescribe where candidate state should be re-measured.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] runCandidate captures the candidate before validation, but after validation it continues using that earlier capture's Tree, BaseTree, and Paths while using the returned post-validation diff. (internal/workflow/engine.go:Engine.runCandidate) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Engine.validate runs configured mutating formatters first, re-reads the resulting diff, and binds subsequent validation evidence to that post-format diff digest. (internal/workflow/engine.go:Engine.validate) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] CandidateCapture freezes a canonical tree, derives its rendered diff from that tree, and carries the exact changed-path set and base tree in the same capture. (internal/gitx/capture.go:Repo.CandidateCapture) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] validation.Bundle.Certifies rejects a candidate-id or diff-digest mismatch and also requires every contained check to certify the same identity. (internal/validation/evidence.go:Bundle.Certifies) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The review verdict records the binding's CandidateTree, reviewedTreeFor supplies that verdict-bound tree to minting, and mintCandidateIdentity re-captures the worktree before minting. (internal/workflow/engine.go:reportReview; internal/workflow/receipt.go:reviewedTreeFor; internal/workflow/mint.go:Engine.mintCandidateIdentity) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] mintCandidateIdentity already refuses a re-captured tree that differs from the verdict-bound tree and independently verifies the canonical commit's reconstruction, tree, and first parent. (internal/workflow/mint.go:Engine.mintCandidateIdentity) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Existing mint tests cover successful canonical identity, absent review identity, verdict-tree disagreement, and movement after review, but do not exercise a configured formatter that mutates candidate bytes before review. (internal/workflow/mint_test.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The configured validation surface supports executable formatter commands, and validation.Runner executes them in the candidate workspace. (internal/config/config.go:Validation; internal/validation/evidence.go:Runner.one) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei identifies reviewer coverage of the whole candidate and revision-bound adversarial verdicts as active critical invariants. (candidate capture and review binding) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] A task-scoped briefing was unavailable; Sensei returned exactly: no task session exists in this repository. The scoped file briefing and preflight remained available and authoritative. (Sensei task session) — source: graph\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: bounded-knowledge-gap\n"}
