{"id":"20260830T074428.979504906Z-16964b70","time":"2026-08-30T07:44:28.979504906Z","session_id":"session-20260830T072521.605271812Z","task_id":"task-1788074721605515483","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  Fix the candidate-identity behaviour when validation mutates candidate bytes, such as when a configured formatter changes a file. The exact candidate tree bound to review must represent the post-validation content the reviewer actually receives. If that exact reviewed state is accepted and does not subsequently move, canonical candidate minting must succeed for that state. A candidate that changes after the state bound to the verdict must still be refused rather than silently rebound. Add a regression test using a validation formatter that actually mutates candidate content and proves the end-to-end identity behaviour. Preserve the existing fail-closed behaviour for candidate movement and do not weaken review-to-tree or base-to-candidate identity checks. Choose the implementation that best preserves the existing authority and identity model; the task does not prescribe where candidate state should be re-measured.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] The scoped preflight for internal/workflow/engine.go and internal/workflow/engine_test.go is authoritative and current, reports ARCHITECTURE_SENSITIVE with local blast radius and no approval gate, and indexes both planned files. (revised two-file implementation envelope) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Engine.runCandidate captures before validation, replaces only the diff returned by Engine.validate, and then currently reads Paths, Tree, and BaseTree from the earlier capture. (internal/workflow/engine.go:Engine.runCandidate) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Engine.validate runs configured formatters first, rereads the resulting candidate diff, and binds the certifying validation bundle to that final diff digest. (internal/workflow/engine.go:Engine.validate) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] CandidateCapture constructs one canonical tree, derives its exact changed-path set after exclusions, and renders the review diff from that tree. (internal/gitx/capture.go:Repo.CandidateCapture) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] mintCandidateIdentity remeasures the worktree against the recorded base, requires equality with the verdict-bound tree, verifies the canonical commit, and separately verifies its tree and first parent. (internal/workflow/mint.go:Engine.mintCandidateIdentity) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The existing mint tests prove successful canonical minting and refusal after post-review movement, while the missing case is the workflow seam where validation itself mutates content before review. (internal/workflow/mint_test.go:TestAnAcceptedCandidateAcquiresAnExactIdentity and TestACandidateThatMovedAfterReviewIsRefused) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] internal/workflow/engine_test.go is an existing indexed workflow test surface containing regression tests for runCandidate ordering, candidate-base pinning, and fail-closed workflow behavior. (internal/workflow/engine_test.go) — source: repository\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: architectural-authority-granted\n"}
{"id":"20260830T074428.979738171Z-3d586cf5","time":"2026-08-30T07:44:28.979738171Z","session_id":"session-20260830T072521.605271812Z","task_id":"task-1788074721605515483","source":"architect","kind":"plan.proposed","summary":"Bind every downstream candidate identity to one canonical post-validation capture, while preserving mint-time movement, reviewed-tree, canonical-commit, and base-parent refusals.\n\nPlan:\n  1. Add a fail-closed post-validation capture in internal/workflow/engine.go that verifies the validation bundle and returned diff against the capture’s canonical rendering.\n  2. Replace downstream uses of the pre-validation capture with the verified post-validation diff, tree, base tree, and path set.\n  3. Add an engine regression using a formatter that actually rewrites candidate content; prove the accepted post-validation tree mints canonically and a later worktree mutation is refused.\n  4. Run gofmt -w cmd internal, go vet ./..., and go test ./... including the focused regression.","payload":{"decision":"proceed","summary":"Bind every downstream candidate identity to one canonical post-validation capture, while preserving mint-time movement, reviewed-tree, canonical-commit, and base-parent refusals.","steps":["Add a fail-closed post-validation capture in internal/workflow/engine.go that verifies the validation bundle and returned diff against the capture’s canonical rendering.","Replace downstream uses of the pre-validation capture with the verified post-validation diff, tree, base tree, and path set.","Add an engine regression using a formatter that actually rewrites candidate content; prove the accepted post-validation tree mints canonically and a later worktree mutation is refused.","Run gofmt -w cmd internal, go vet ./..., and go test ./... including the focused regression."],"consequences":"Formatting may change candidate identity before review, but audit, review, evidence, receipts, reporting, and minting will all name the same post-validation state. Content changed after the verdict remains unmintable, and no review-to-tree or base-to-candidate check is weakened.","files":["internal/workflow/engine.go","internal/workflow/engine_test.go"],"mode":"modify","related_invariants":["invariant:sensei_code.roles.adversarial_roles_inherit_nothing_and_bind_to_a_revision","invariant:sensei_code.candidate.reviewer_sees_every_changed_file"],"plan":"After validation, canonically re-capture the candidate against its recorded base and declared paths. Refuse unless the validation bundle certifies that capture’s rendered diff and the returned validation diff agrees with it. Use the refreshed capture’s diff, tree, base tree, and exact paths for audit, review, receipts, reporting, decision recording, and minting. Leave the mint’s independent remeasurement and canonical identity checks unchanged.","claims":[{"statement":"The scoped preflight for internal/workflow/engine.go and internal/workflow/engine_test.go is authoritative and current, reports ARCHITECTURE_SENSITIVE with local blast radius and no approval gate, and indexes both planned files.","about":"revised two-file implementation envelope","source":"graph"},{"statement":"Engine.runCandidate captures before validation, replaces only the diff returned by Engine.validate, and then currently reads Paths, Tree, and BaseTree from the earlier capture.","about":"internal/workflow/engine.go:Engine.runCandidate","source":"repository"},{"statement":"Engine.validate runs configured formatters first, rereads the resulting candidate diff, and binds the certifying validation bundle to that final diff digest.","about":"internal/workflow/engine.go:Engine.validate","source":"repository"},{"statement":"CandidateCapture constructs one canonical tree, derives its exact changed-path set after exclusions, and renders the review diff from that tree.","about":"internal/gitx/capture.go:Repo.CandidateCapture","source":"repository"},{"statement":"mintCandidateIdentity remeasures the worktree against the recorded base, requires equality with the verdict-bound tree, verifies the canonical commit, and separately verifies its tree and first parent.","about":"internal/workflow/mint.go:Engine.mintCandidateIdentity","source":"repository"},{"statement":"The existing mint tests prove successful canonical minting and refusal after post-review movement, while the missing case is the workflow seam where validation itself mutates content before review.","about":"internal/workflow/mint_test.go:TestAnAcceptedCandidateAcquiresAnExactIdentity and TestACandidateThatMovedAfterReviewIsRefused","source":"repository"},{"statement":"internal/workflow/engine_test.go is an existing indexed workflow test surface containing regression tests for runCandidate ordering, candidate-base pinning, and fail-closed workflow behavior.","about":"internal/workflow/engine_test.go","source":"repository"}],"premise_resolutions":[{"gap":"gap-1788074721605515483-1","outcome":"refuted","evidence":"The revised plan does not edit internal/workflow/mint_test.go. Repository inspection located the defect in internal/workflow/engine.go:Engine.runCandidate, and the regression is moved to existing internal/workflow/engine_test.go; scoped preflight reports both revised files indexed."},{"gap":"gap-1788074721605515483-2","outcome":"refuted","evidence":"The revised plan removes internal/workflow/mint_test.go from the mutation envelope. internal/workflow/engine_test.go already tests runCandidate ordering and base pinning and is indexed in the authoritative scoped preflight."},{"gap":"gap-1788074721605515483-3","outcome":"refuted","evidence":"The uncovered test file is no longer planned. The exact revised scope is internal/workflow/engine.go plus internal/workflow/engine_test.go, for which Sensei reports 2 files indexed out of 2 with sufficient coverage."}],"plan_source":"architect"}}
