{"id":"20260830T075501.218691175Z-b0a03f1a","time":"2026-08-30T07:55:01.218691175Z","session_id":"session-20260830T072521.605271812Z","task_id":"task-1788074721605515483","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01J4Zmuruotk8KSTT3KMYGVK\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"372-\\tDetail      string `json:\\\"detail\\\"`\\n373-\\tMessage     string `json:\\\"message\\\"`\\n374-}\\n375-\\n376-// DiffAuditDecision is the typed form of awareness_audit_diff.\\n377:type DiffAuditDecision struct {\\n378-\\tSchema          string            `json:\\\"schema\\\"`\\n379-\\tDigest          string            `json:\\\"digest\\\"`\\n380-\\tInputDiffDigest string            `json:\\\"input_diff_digest\\\"`\\n381-\\tAvailability    AuditAvailability `json:\\\"availability\\\"`\\n382-\\tDecision        AuditDecision     `json:\\\"decision\\\"`\\n383-\\tExpectedHead    string            `json:\\\"expected_head\\\"`\\n384-\\tDomain          string            `json:\\\"domain\\\"`\\n385-\\tGraphCommit     string            `json:\\\"graph_commit\\\"`\\n386-\\tFindings        []AuditFinding    `json:\\\"findings\\\"`\\n387-\\tReasonCodes     []string          `json:\\\"reason_codes\\\"`\\n388-\\tLimitations     []string          `json:\\\"limitations\\\"`\\n389-}\\n390-\\n391-// ReviewerMayAccept reports whether a reviewer's acceptance is allowed to\\n392-// stand, which is a different question from whether the audit passed.\\n393-//\\n394-// Sensei's four verdicts mean different things about who decides. pass and\\n395-// review both leave room for judgement — review means precisely \\\"a reviewer\\n396-// must look at this\\\". block does not: it is Sensei's refusal, and a reviewer\\n397-// accepting over it would make the reviewer the effective judge of an\\n398-// architectural audit, which is the authority inversion this whole gate\\n399-// exists to prevent. cannot_verify is not a pass