h\":0,\"spawned_by_subagents\":0,\"completed\":0,\"failed\":0,\"killed\":{\"parent\":0,\"user\":0,\"system\":0},\"refused\":{\"depth_limit\":0,\"concurrency_limit\":0,\"budget\":0},\"by_type\":{}},\"is_error\":false,\"num_turns\":77,\"subtype\":\"success\",\"api_error_status\":null,\"result\":\"The blocking review finding is reconciled: there is now a regression that drives the real production loop.\\n\\n## What changed (this cycle: `internal/workflow/postvalidation_test.go` only)\\n\\n**Added `TestTheGovernedLoopBindsTheCandidateTheFormatterProduced`** — it calls `runCandidate` itself, with three deterministic processes served by re-entering the test binary (`TestPostValidationStubProcess`):\\n\\n- an **implementor** that writes `println( 1 )` — Go that gofmt will rewrite, so validation performs a real mutation;\\n- an **independent reviewer** (`codex` vs the `claude` worker, so `roles.Assign` is satisfied) that records the prompt it received and accepts;\\n- a **Sensei MCP stub** speaking the real Content-Length JSON-RPC framing `internal/sensei` expects, which records the diff handed to `awareness_audit_diff` and returns `decision=pass / availability=available`.\\n\\nThe candidate is a real git worktree cut from the recorded base; the loop's own guard install, capture, `gofmt -w` / `gofmt -l` validation, audit, review packet and verdict recording all run unmodified.\\n\\nIt then asserts, against the formatter-produced capture:\\n- the diff Sensei audited is byte-equal to the post-validation rendering;\\n- the reviewer's prompt contains `println(1)`, never `println( 1 )`, and names the post-validation revision;\\n- the delivered verdict's tree (`reviewedTreeFor`) and digest (`reviewedDigestFor`) are the post-validation capture's;\\n- `tc.EvidenceSnapshot.ChangedPaths` is the capture's exact path set;\\n- `mintCandidateIdentity` succeeds and the minted commit reconstructs canonically from `(base, reviewed tree)`;\\n- after a later worktree mutation, the mint refuses with \\\"moved after it was reviewed\\\".\\n\\n**Mutation-checked, not assumed:** with `capture, diff = reviewed, reviewed.Diff` removed from `runCandidate`, the test fails — `the verdict is bound to tree 24a5e07800c0 and the reviewed state is b7102cf62e1c`. Restored afterwards; `engine.go` is byte-identical to what cycle 1 produced.\\n\\n**Removed `TestTheTreeAFormatterProducedIsTheTreeThatMints`.** That was the test the review named as overclaiming: it hand-assembled the sequence and installed the tree into the receipt itself. The new loop test covers the same ground for real. `TestThePreValidationCaptureIsNotTheReviewedState` and `TestValidationEvidenceAboutOtherBytesIsRefused` are kept — their claims are narrow and true.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n```\\ngofmt -w cmd internal   # clean\\ngo vet ./...            # clean\\ngo test ./...           # all packages ok\\ngo test ./internal/workflow/ -count=2   # ok\\ngo test ./internal/workflow/ -race -run 'TestTheGovernedLoop|...'  # ok\\n```\\n\\nThe test skips if `gofmt` is not on PATH, since without a real rewrite it distinguishes nothing.\\n\\n## Not done, deliberately\\n\\nNo `sensei propose` entry was added for this failure class — the bounded plan's four steps do not include graph feedback, and that is the architect's call, not mine. If wanted, the natural shape is a `failure_mode` for \\\"downstream identity bound to the pre-validation capture\\\" plus a `required_test` pointing at `internal/workflow/postvalidation_test.go:TestTheGovernedLoopBindsTheCandidateTheFormatterProduced`.\\n\\nAWG: briefing(internal/workflow/engine.go) | invariants: sensei_code.roles.adversarial_roles_inherit_nothing_and_bind_to_a_revision, sensei_code.workflow.context_never_widens_worker_scope | uncertainty: the stub MCP/provider processes exercise the loop's identity path faithfully but pass every audit, so this proves binding, not judgement\",\"ttft_ms\":3064,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":695505,\"uuid\":\"d723b564-e960-415f-9038-8f96d1edad34\",\"ttft_stream_ms\":2140,\"time_to_request_ms\":58,\"queued_turn_count\":0}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
